[size=5][b]Living Chrome[/b][/size]
[i]Your cyberware isn't just installed. It grows, it has quirks, and sometimes it fights back.[/i]

Every implant you equip earns XP as you use it, levels from 1 to 5, and rolls a hidden personality the first time you install it. Max it out and it masters. Get a Glitchy one and it learns twice as fast but may short-circuit in the middle of a firefight, unless you pay a ripperdoc to stabilize it.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Implants level up (1-5)[/b] from combat time, nearby kills, and from [b]doing their own job[/b]:
[list]
[*]Frontal Cortex / Operating System: spending RAM on quickhacks. The OS also learns from Sandevistan and Berserk activations.
[*]Nervous System: Kerenzikov activations
[*]Eyes / Hands / Arms: kills
[*]Skeleton / Immune / Integumentary: taking damage
[*]Circulatory System: healing
[*]Legs / Arms: spending stamina (dashing, melee)
[/list]
[*][b]Bonuses per level[/b] by body area: Crit Chance, Crit Damage, Max Health, Armor or Max Stamina.
[*][b]Mastery at Lv 5:[/b] every implant adds a second bonus (e.g. +2 Max RAM for the OS, +10 Armor for the Skeleton).
[*][b]Quirks[/b], rolled once per implant:
[list]
[*][b]Clean[/b] (60%): normal chrome
[*][b]Tuned[/b] (25%): learns 50% faster
[*][b]Glitchy[/b] (15%): learns 2x faster with 25% bigger bonuses, but malfunctions in combat until Lv 5 or until a ripperdoc stabilizes it
[/list]
[*][b]Malfunctions depend on where the implant sits[/b] (6 seconds each):
[list]
[*]Eyes: OPTICS FAULT (screen glitch, -15% Crit Chance)
[*]Frontal Cortex / OS: RAM LEAK (screen glitch, RAM emptied)
[*]Nervous System / Legs: MOTOR STUTTER (Stamina emptied)
[*]Body systems: PLATING FAULT (-100 Armor)
[*]Hands / Arms: SERVO JAM (Crit Damage and Crit Chance penalties)
[/list]
[*][b]Ripperdoc services:[/b] with a ripperdoc's screen open, open the CET overlay to pay eddies to [b]stabilize[/b] a Glitchy implant (6000) or [b]re-roll[/b] a quirk (3000).
[*][b]Living Chrome window[/b] in the CET overlay: implants grouped by quirk, level, XP bar, bonus, mastery, kills, STABLE / MASTERED tags.
[*][b]Settings[/b] in the window, and in the game's Settings menu if you use Native Settings UI: XP rates, malfunction chance and length, screen glitch on/off, on-screen messages, ripperdoc prices.
[*][b]Per-playthrough progress:[/b] every playthrough keeps its own implant levels and quirks. Upgrading an implant to a higher tier keeps its progress.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 patch 2.5
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/107]Cyber Engine Tweaks[/url] 1.38 or newer
[*]Optional: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/3518]Native Settings UI[/url] for a Living Chrome tab in the game's Settings
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Install with Vortex, or manually: extract the zip into your Cyberpunk 2077 folder (the one with [i]bin[/i] and [i]archive[/i]) and merge folders. You should end up with:
[code]Cyberpunk 2077\bin\x64\plugins\cyber_engine_tweaks\mods\LivingChrome\init.lua[/code]
When the game starts, the CET console says [i][Living Chrome] v0.3.0 loaded.[/i]

[size=4][b]Save safety / uninstalling[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Stat bonuses and malfunction penalties are [b]never written into your save[/b]. The mod re-applies bonuses each time you load.
[*]The only thing stored in your save is a hidden ID number that the game ignores.
[*]The malfunction screen glitch is tracked so that a save made mid-glitch is cleaned up on the next load, and the mod never touches the story's own copy of that effect.
[*]Clean uninstall: in the CET console run [code]GetMod("LivingChrome").uninstall()[/code] then save, quit, and delete the LivingChrome folder.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Console commands[/b][/size] (CET console)
[code]GetMod("LivingChrome").status()                  list implants and progress
GetMod("LivingChrome").addXp(500)                give equipped implants XP (testing)
GetMod("LivingChrome").forceMalfunction("limbs") test a malfunction: optics, cortex, neural, body, limbs
GetMod("LivingChrome").clearGlitch()             remove a stuck malfunction screen glitch
GetMod("LivingChrome").reset()                   wipe progress for this playthrough
GetMod("LivingChrome").uninstall()               remove all bonuses before uninstalling[/code]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
Works alongside Cyberware-EX (extra slots) and Wannabe Edgerunner. The mod only adds its own temporary stat bonuses and doesn't edit any game files or items.

[size=4][b]Reporting problems[/b][/size]
Please post the red lines from the CET console, or the end of [i]bin\x64\plugins\cyber_engine_tweaks\scripting.log[/i], in the Posts tab.

Source code: [url=https://github.com/La2o/Cyberpunk2077-LivingChrome]GitHub[/url]

[i]This mod was made with AI assistance.[/i]
